From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: oleaut32: Read complete MSFT type description offsets.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

Windows 10 x86_64/i686 loads our public-API-generated library with 5000
records and aliases, preserving PTR -> CARRAY -> PTR -> USERDEFINED,
array bounds, record identity and the I4 field. Its own descriptor and
array-description tables contain offsets crossing both 0x8000 and 0x10000.
Wine reads only a signed low word at three reader sites, losing the high
word or addressing before the allocation. Reconstruct the complete offsets.

v2 (2026-11-09): Keep all three production implementation changes unchanged.
Add a reader compatibility test with values from the completed Windows
MEASURE, including object release. Construct only one CARRAY per alias to
avoid an unrelated recursive writer lifetime issue. Audit boundary coverage
read-only and reload a fresh-path copy after releasing the writer. The test
asserts returned types, bounds, record identity and field type, not numeric
HREFTYPE handles. No invalid-input fallback behaviour is asserted. Native
assertion L1, paired L2 and formal cross review remain pending.

